\lispPackageChapter{candlesticks/config}

The \texttt{candlesticks/config} package holds the connection helpers and
the small conversions every other package needs.  A connection spec is a
list that \texttt{postmodern:connect} can be applied to, for example
\path{("database" "user" "password" "host" :port 5432)}.

\section{Variables}

\lispVariableSubsection{*default-connection-spec*}

The spec \texttt{with-connection} uses when it is not given one.  Initially
\texttt{nil}.  Set it with \texttt{set-default-connection-spec!}, or bind
it around a call.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{default-connection-spec}

The current value of \texttt{*default-connection-spec*}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{set-default-connection-spec!}

Set \texttt{*default-connection-spec*} to \lispVar{spec-list} and return
it.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(set-default-connection-spec! \lispVar{spec-list})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{connection-spec}

Return \lispVar{spec-list}, or \texttt{*default-connection-spec*} when
\lispVar{spec-list} is \texttt{nil}.  Signals an error when neither is
available.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(connection-spec \&optional \lispVar{spec-list})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{current-connection}

The active Postmodern connection, or \texttt{nil} when none is bound.
This is \texttt{postmodern:*database*}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{connected-p}

True if \lispVar{connection} (default: the active connection) is open and
connected.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(connected-p \&optional \lispVar{connection})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{require-connection!}

Return the active Postmodern connection, signalling a clear error if there
is none.

\lispFunctionSubsection{universal-time->timestamptz}

Format a universal time as a PostgreSQL \texttt{timestamptz} literal in
\textsc{Utc}, e.g.\ \texttt{"2026-08-18 12:00:00+00"}.  This is the form
Postmodern and PostgreSQL accept as a parameter.  When such a value is
read back, Postmodern hands it to us as a universal time again.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(universal-time->timestamptz \lispVar{universal-time})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{canonicalize-slug}

Trim leading and trailing whitespace from a name and down-case it, so that
\texttt{"API"}, \texttt{" api "}, and \texttt{"Api"} are the same slug.
Used for instrument type names and data source kind names.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(canonicalize-slug \lispVar{name})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{to-db}

Convert a Lisp \texttt{nil} into the Postmodern \textsc{Null} marker
\texttt{:null}.  Any other value is returned unchanged.

\lispFunctionSubsection{from-db}

Convert a Postmodern \texttt{:null} into Lisp \texttt{nil}.  Any other
value is returned unchanged.

\lispFunctionSubsection{coerce-price}

Coerce a numeric value read back from the database (Postmodern returns
\texttt{numeric} columns as rationals) into a float.  \texttt{nil} and
\texttt{:null} pass through as \texttt{nil}, so nullable columns such as
volume stay \texttt{nil}.

\section{Macros}

\lispMacroSubsection{with-connection}

Evaluate \lispVar{body} with the active database connection bound to a
connection opened from \lispVar{spec-list}.  When \lispVar{spec-list} is
\texttt{nil}, \lispId{*default-connection-spec*} is used instead.  The
connection is closed when \lispVar{body} finishes.  Nesting or repeating
the form gives you several independent connections.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(with-connection \lispVar{spec-list} \&body \lispVar{body})}}

\lispExamples

\begin{lstlisting}
(with-connection '("db" "user" "pw" "localhost" :port 5432)
  (all-instruments))

(let ((*default-connection-spec* '("db" "user" "pw" "localhost" :port 5432)))
  (with-connection nil
    (all-instruments)))
\end{lstlisting}

\lispMacroSubsection{first-row}

Run a parameterized \textsc{Sql} statement and return the first row as a
list of values, or \texttt{nil} when there is no row.  This is a macro so
that its parameters are compile-time forms, which is what Postmodern's
\texttt{query} macro requires.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(first-row \lispVar{sql} \&rest \lispVar{params})}}
